[statement]
Observed; the rule is not yet known in full. As
`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-passed-over-beside-one-depending-on-its-requirer`,
where the candidate depends on a package the request names beside the
requirer: `b` needs `a`, `a` 3 needs `missing`, `a` 1 needs `z`, and `b`
and `z` are requested; apk installs `a` 1. Where `z` is needed beside `b`
by a package, apk refuses
(`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-not-passed-over-for-a-package-beside-the-chain`).

[repository]
P:z
V:1

P:a
V:1
D:z

P:a
V:3
D:missing

P:b
V:2
D:a

[request]
b
z

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install z 1
install a 1
install b 2
